The diagram is drawn on a square grid. Is $KL \perp MN$ true or false? Consider the full lines if the segments are extended.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{gridcolour}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[step=0.5,draw=gridcolour,thin] (-2.5,-2) grid (2.5,2);
\draw[thick] (-1.5,-1.5) node[below left] {$K$} -- (-1.5,1.5) node[above left] {$L$};
\draw[thick] (0,-0.5) node[below] {$M$} -- (2,-0.5) node[below] {$N$};
\draw[thick] (-0.5,-1.5) node[below] {$P$} -- (2,1) node[above] {$Q$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
True. $KL$ follows a vertical grid line and $MN$ follows a horizontal grid line. Their full lines meet at $90^{\circ}$.

$KL \perp MN$

The dashed extension and square below show their right-angle meeting point.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{gridcolour}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[step=0.5,draw=gridcolour,thin] (-2.5,-2) grid (2.5,2);
\draw[thick] (-1.5,-1.5) node[below left] {$K$} -- (-1.5,1.5) node[above left] {$L$};
\draw[thick] (0,-0.5) node[below] {$M$} -- (2,-0.5) node[below] {$N$};
\draw[thick] (-0.5,-1.5) node[below] {$P$} -- (2,1) node[above] {$Q$};
\draw[dashed] (-1.5,-0.5) -- (0,-0.5);
\draw (-1.22,-0.5) -- (-1.22,-0.22) -- (-1.5,-0.22);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

